**/target
**/Cargo.lock
# task-manager-rest-api's lock IS committed, and the pre-baked builder image is why — see
# .github/workflows/build-task-manager-rest-api-docker.yaml. With the lock ignored, CI resolves fresh and
# takes the newest semver-compatible release of every transitive crate, so one patch published anywhere in
# a ~400-crate graph invalidates the image and the warm build silently becomes a cold one. Committing it
# also means a broken transitive dependency reproduces locally instead of only in CI.
#
# The UI lock is also tracked so deployment bundles use the same graph as the tested WASM build.
!task-manager-rest-api/Cargo.lock
!task-manager-ui/Cargo.lock
**/dist
.claude
.idea
.DS_Store
.mcp.json
